849:- **Havel:** the sixth sheet, the last.
852:- **Fifth sitting (day 82, documentary):** the records' contents leaf read; the maker attests ("I made them. They are true.", with the seventh-week correction noted); the enrollee attests ("They are mine."); the advocate of record signs the receipt. No question from the petitioner. The road not reported.
858:- **Advanced:** the first pole (dead — "the room was never the system"; no second pole yet); Seln's deciding (decided); Karis's curve; Ephram's watching; Brom's sealed letter (still sealed); Havel (closed at six).
859:- **Closed:** the reach priced and paid; the fifth sitting; the district seat's answer; Havel's note (six, the last); Storm's resettling.
860:- **Plants (kept at altitude):** Seln's twelve-years-ago press — "paper that was entirely correct in every particular, and that sat a little above where it should have sat, and had been put there by somebody who could reach" (ch29) — rhymes with the fourteenth lot; no content, no *falsification*. Havel's first and sixth sheets side by side (a mark with no office; a seal with no register) — nothing made of them.
863:- (a) **The trip's shape** is the flood: the town ferry tied up and Ostrand bridge chained at the third ring force the coach round by an upper chain ferry at a narrows two hours west, and back east along the far bank's river road through the cut (west of Ostrand, two hours short — §11 #7). The faction chose a day with one road.
864:- (b) The cut is in wind after rain; "road dust" is the cut's chalk (the ferryman: it drinks the rain and blows dry in an hour). Geese once, no season word.
865:- (c) **Seln's absence** is given a concrete act: under the team's wagon in the gully, taking its linchpin. He sees nothing of the reach.
868:- (f) **The postponement** is Seln posting the next week's schedule a day early with the five moved to day 88; the original First-day plan (day 85) never went up on a board.
870:- (h) The birthday is in **the reading room** (tomorrow's room), so Seln's line about the room is about where he will open the case.
872:- (j) Cutaways: Seln ~5.6k (packet ~5k), Havel ~2.0k (packet ~2k).
876:- **Anchor in use (flag):** points fixed against a surface (ground, stone, a jamb, a horse's foreleg, a coat); invisible; the read finds a laid point as "weight with no body"; lines (courses) between points, found by touch, frayed by heat (Karis) and by Cael's spark (one thread); points laid where the target's half beat says it will go; points accumulate and are not lifted; range costs a half-second's stillness ("threading a needle"); a **cage** is points close round a body laid through a **first point set against the body**; a closed cage is a hold; **released from inside** by letting the first point go, the cage and every point threaded through it unthread in the order laid. Consistent with B7's "can release a laid point from inside" and "wants doorways".
877:- **The fourteen (flag):** two on the milestone, one on each culvert parapet, three high in the north bank, two in the south lip, three across the west mouth (flush; the coach rolled over them), three in the road; a frame closed at both mouths with one twelve-foot channel along the south bank to the culvert.
878:- **The cut (flag):** chalk; ~440 yards; north bank twenty feet with a ditch below, south bank ten–twelve feet, **undercut near the east end**; cambered road twenty-odd feet wide; culvert, low parapets, milestone *seven* to the city; two bends up from the ferry landing through hawthorn.
881:- **The team (flag):** six — a lead (counts the drill), four (two heavier), the woman; grey road clothes, hoods, scarves to the eyes; staves, soft rope, hobbles, a folded hood; no blades; a closed wagon with a barred back, a bench and two floor rings, its horses tied up the stream. The woman's **grey eyes** (minor).
884:- **Seln (flag):** four favours in fifteen years (the mould-room man; the western-stores woman; a coastal ferry-master; a retired officer of his service, never to be spent); two spent; the drop at a ship's chandler's near the bridge; the **quick bag**; registry sample leaves in the back of his second manual; **the four grades** (record, instrument, knock, hand) and the catechism taught by an old woman with a stick and a cat in a room over a chandler's on a quay, to six recruits; the catechism said on nineteen first mornings; his weekly return's text (ch29).
886:- **Havel (flag):** the district seat's records room a man short; the impression book (red wafers); the printed schedule of seals of office (grey binding, yearly); the cutters' issue ledger (three cutters; the rim number in the beading; a copy in every district strong-room); the rubbing's number falls between a southern ferry office's die and an eastern fee office's, consecutive; the facilities office's instrument bears the same seal; the reply's text; the sixth sheet's text.
889:- **The second set of copies** kept in the annex; the seventh-week card corrected in the desk clerk's ink, with Seln's margin.
