   169	He had thought about how to say it all day, and in the end he said it plainly, because there was no way to say it that would make it smaller. On the night of the gate Lira had written her question in capitals in her notebook and left it lying open in the middle of the table, what do they try next, when paper won't do it, and nobody had answered it. He did not have an answer now either. But there was one thing he could do about the question before it was answered, and that was to price it.
