editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/movement-004/compiled-prompt.md:457:On the second of those afternoons, at the outer edge of the circle, Cael saw a small wiry figure in a Current smock with her hair dried into a wild bush. It was the first-year from the third ring, seventy-fourth on the Copper sheet, standing on her toes behind two Blade fourth-years to hear what the best fighter on the bluff thought about a bout she would never be in. Nobody had told her she could not reach the final. Nobody had told her she was allowed to listen to Ephram, either. She had simply come, and was listening, with her lips moving. Cael found, to his surprise, that he was glad.
