editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md-27-- **The reading taught on the road:** "Well?" / "May I read you?" / "Yes…" Surface at ten: Tide *there*, the first thing that has ever been there at ten. A minute of the long one: banks, one channel, a current that runs *to* things. "You're built to arrive." / "Yes… That's what I am." "He asked twice and got one." / "That's the rate."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md-28-- **The Stair from the ridge at dusk:** a bowl wider and shallower than the Ring's; a bare floor with no ring; a square hole with three lit steps and then dark. The line at forty paces ("Two hundred. I'll pace it in the morning."). **Two stakes numbered thirty-two**, one under five winters of scale and one under one or two, with the **stroke and the bar**: "Newer. This one's been re-surveyed." Camp at the line.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:29:- **Day 114, the trap (≈9,000–10,500 across two chapters).** The crossing in Seln's order. **The bolt at forty meters**: "Ridge." Six hooded on the rim in road grey (two south, two east, one west, one north). **The Anchor course** closing the line behind them; Cael sees it with perception only. Bolts skip off the fused plate. **Lira runs *down***, and the unit follows. **Forty steps.** The chamber, ten strides square, its ceiling the floor; walls carved; at the middle "something cased… a cord," unread. **The doorway**: "They can shoot the bowl… They can't shoot the stair." **Oryn without hands**: lamp, eyes, two fingers; "Tape it. Leave the bolt."; "the bolt's the plug"; "I came south for exactly this. Enter that." Lira's mend reopened on the stair wall. **The stalemate, given room**: the square of grey going white and grey; a bolt sent down to stop at the thirty-first step; Brom grey and not worse; Karis with her back to the wall she would give a year to read. The design read aloud ("It thinks the floor did the same thing to all six of us."). **The order:** up alone with the one he was given. Oryn: "Ask first." / "I'm not reading anyone." / "I know. I'm saying the rule out loud so it's been said on this floor too." Lira: "Later." **The ascent, Shadow alone**, across the bowl unseen; the rim scanning for a shout that cannot exist. Anchor let off at ten meters as perception, then as a hand: **the knot found and released**, the course going slack like rigging. **Over the stone, declaring**: Wind, Storm seeding the rut, Compression at contact, Ember held out. He removes one man from the plan and does not fight him. The rim breaks as professionals break. The west one looks back for a second, hood up, nothing in it. Four crossbows left; no faces. "Back."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md-30-- **Out at dark:** "There. Back… The clock started again." The bolt-head cut and the shaft drawn; an hour on Brom; a quarter on Lira ("It held a stair…"). His bill: the suite spent on a week's rest. **Seln breaks a stock across the stone**: "No faces." The log (protected). **Teague's crew at full dark** (protected exchange); he does not ask how.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md-31-- **Day 115:** Teague holds the rim unasked ("We'll hold it till you're up." / "Noted"). **C3: Karis paces the Stair's perimeter in the morning** with Lira one-armed on the line, under four rim-holders who are theirs, and gets two hundred. **Down with two lamps**: the air at the twentieth step; the chamber catalogued properly; Oryn's "What are they" / "Lines." **The kit**: open, contents in taking-out order, the cord laid toward the east wall, stake thirty-two with the stroke-and-bar beside its mallet, point bright, the floor unmarked (EXC-B7-004: "Twice, by the head… Nothing goes into this."). **The ledger read by Seln**: distances, the radius in their own hand, a designation in an index he does not know, and the last line, *third site confirmed on bearing* —. **Karis's body at "bearing."** Six hours; twenty-nine sheets; "Sheet"; Lira ahead of her every time; **forty-one** (protected); the line *between* the courses at the radius; "A measurement is a fact about a ruler…" **The kit carried up**: Brom refuses help three times. The rim-holders: the spear grounded once. The log at the stone (protected). The straightedge out on the carter's map, not yet touching anything.
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md-24-- **The herd and Karis's day** as a full learning encounter: spacing; the line moved without an animal seen moving; a rock passing between two of them (a step, not flight); the plate going and the herd stepping uphill *as one, no first animal*. Laid beside the ford page: same sense, opposite answer. "Derived. Not tested." "On a slope, flight is a landslide with legs." "Write it in yours, too. I'd like it in two hands."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md-25-- **The narrowings** and the eighth's clean break. Brom takes the cart across it, and the tail-board doesn't bang because nobody lets it. The ledge in sight. "I'll run it at first light."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:26:- **The ledge and the stampede (≈4,500, terrain fight):** the ledge goes under Lira; her own Wind, full, crosses the gorge; thirty heads come up; the shelf cannot hold them at a run, and they come down the face in a front. "There. Thirty seconds. Lee side." "Cart's gone." **Karis's lattice line** across the face is a declaration the size of a road. The herd splits round the fin at eleven paces; she sits down at the eighth second, emptied. Brom goes back for two boxes (the wrist goes under the cloth). Cael goes after the third. Compression and Anchor *want*, and he prices both and holds, because the split stands on Karis's line and one more loud thing turns it. He takes the shoulder raw: three ribs, left side, low; the calf opened on the shale. The cart floats and goes in with its shafts up. Lira's leg broken under a plate, the boot gone. "That was me… The loud thing." / "It was the ledge. The ledge went. Then it was you." / "Then it was me."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md-27-- **The fin's lee, days 78–79, on the page:** rationing; the lip walked by Seln; the fan still sliding; Lira's leg hot under the plates; Karis unable to light a lamp; nobody writes.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md-28-- **Day 80, Oryn**, introduced through her walk and then her hands: "Who's worst?"; the set ("That's the part you'll mind"); the mend in less than an hour (Lira: "Cold… No. It's going along."); she sits as a carter sets down a known load; "That's one."; "Hands on. That's the only way it works… And I can't do it to me."; Brom's wrist ("Then it should have closed in a month and hasn't, because you've pulled on it."); Karis: "Ember. And nothing. You're empty."; "Hm." at the lattice line. **The first failed surface reading** on Cael: she stops in the middle, looks at her hands, tries again, and her face does the instrument's thing. The protected exchange ends on "That's a *finding*."
--
