editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:184:| **The hold** (method; not a fragment) | M1 taught as a discipline and given failure modes (Shadow drifting at dusk, Anchor's wants); M2 inverted at the ford (bait with one, kill with everything that isn't one); M5 dropped all at once inside the Ring | A sequence of small refusals, "arriving faster than a person could name them" |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md-185-| **Observation on animals** (method) | M1 the stretch (five items); M2 the ford's first mover; M3 the herd (no first mover; flight); M5 inside the Ring the pack is careless, because no prey there has ever shouted | Finds seams; names nothing it cannot count |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md-186-| **Wind-adjacent** | M2 one burst, openly, at the ford (the landing lock with a dog in it); M4 a foot's worth of evasion, silent, twenty strides inside the line (private); M5 two full bursts inside the Ring; M7 on the Stair's rim | The fixed one-count landing lock; never spend a burst near an opponent whose single hit he cannot price |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md-187-| **Iron-adjacent read** | M1–M3 held, even on the stretch; M4 run privately across the line and on the floor ("no seam"); M5 under his soles the whole retreat; M8 under water at the Hall ("the read at its dearest") | About a pace and a half; mass and vector, never intent; cheap and quiet; costs attention under water |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md-188-| **Shadow-adjacent** (sealed) | Drifts at dusk in M1–M4 and is held. **Used exactly twice:** M5 ten strides to reach Karis (circle and Oryn only); M7 up the stair and across the bowl, unseen by the rim, never attributable | Costs from waking; the seal's whole logic is restated once (M2 log) and honored |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:189:| **Anchor-adjacent** | Wants doorways and the stake (idle); M5 perception only (sees Karis's points before they light); M7 the course **unbound from inside**; M8 the trial point, then **one fixed point held on the Hall's floor** | A point fixed *against* a surface; holding it against a biting thing costs "the whole of the rest" |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md-190-| **Compression-adjacent** | M5 a hound taken at contact in the second lock; M7 at contact on the rim; M8 the wyrm's first strike taken into a standing frame | Bill in the ribs (the Hall's, carried into the cold) |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md-191-| **Pressure, Ember, Blade, Storm** | M5 spent as noise in the run (Ember one point held out; Storm seeding the rut; Blade ringing with nothing to cut); M7 the Daeva suite on the rim (Wind, Storm, Compression, Ember) | Storm is the heaviest thing he owns and resettles round any new arrival (M6, heard for the first time) |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md-192-| **Tide-adjacent (NEW, the tenth)** | M5 day 100 the deep reading; **the notice** (verbatim, §10); M6 cost: three days of *listening*, not pulling (his own current at the edge of thought; the nine audible as flows); the idle state learned by the third night; **the first self-reading** (a place near the middle that does not flow; location only; not named); M7 ask refused at the lean-to, granted on the road; the first reading of another person (Oryn: banks, one channel, a current that runs *to* things); M8 the second and third self-readings; **"the still place"** (the phrase appears first here); told to Oryn with his hand on her wrist; **Teague not read** | Contact only; surface at a count of ten, deep only with the subject still, whole and willing; does nothing in a fight; *ask first, every time*; "Things you keep touching don't heal" |
